cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project in research, please cite this repository at the release you used, and the archived release DOI once one is available."
title: "Robot Sports Gym"
type: software
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-09-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/maybe2122/Robot-Sports-Gym"
authors:
  - name: "Robot Sports Gym contributors"
abstract: >-
  A cross-embodiment robot ball-sports training and evaluation platform on
  MuJoCo and Isaac Sim/PhysX. Release 0.3.0 provides five single-shot tasks
  (table-tennis and tennis returns, badminton serve, football kick, basketball
  shoot) with fixed, simulation-verified shot banks, versioned Gymnasium
  environments, frozen L0-L5 criteria, reference and learned baselines, an
  embodied Franka Panda / Unitree G1 table-tennis track with state and vision
  observations, an Isaac Lab environment compared shot by shot with MuJoCo,
  versioned JSON Schemas and an auditable result-package format. All shot banks
  are experimental; no leaderboard is open.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - reinforcement learning
  - MuJoCo
  - Isaac Sim
  - Isaac Lab
  - robot benchmark
  - sports simulation
  - Gymnasium
